---
import ThemeToggle from './ThemeToggle.astro';
import { SITE_SHORT_TITLE } from '../consts';

---

<header class="site-header">
  <a class="site-header__brand" href="/">
    <span class="puck" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    {/*
      The wordmark carries its own class because it, not the link, has to own
      the truncation — see .site-header__name in global.css.
    */}
    <span class="site-header__name">{SITE_SHORT_TITLE}</span>
  </a>
  <span class="site-header__spacer"></span>
  <div class="site-header__actions">
    {/*
      Always the home page, on every page type. It used to take a `navHref`
      prop and point at #site-nav on the document and hub pages, which made
      one button do three different things: a page load on the bare pages, a
      jump to the bottom of the document below 60rem, and above 60rem a
      barely-perceptible nudge of the text and nothing else — reported by a
      reader, and the reason the prop is gone. ⚠️ THE NUDGE'S MECHANISM WAS
      NEVER MEASURED IN A BROWSER, only read off the CSS: the rail is sticky
      at `top: var(--header-h)` while <html> carries
      `scroll-padding-top: calc(var(--header-h) + var(--player-h) + 1rem)`,
      so the target can never clear the padding and the scroll stops a few
      pixels in. Plausible, unverified — do not cite it as measured. What is
      certain is that a cross-page link cannot scroll a fragment at all, so
      the symptom cannot survive this change whatever caused it.

      The deeper reason is not the nudge: a reader cannot learn a button that
      behaves by breakpoint. Home is the contents.
    */}
    <a class="icon-button" href="/">Contents</a>
    <a class="icon-button" href="/search/" rel="search">
      <span aria-hidden="true">⌕</span>
      {/*
        Below 31rem this label is hidden visually but kept for assistive
        technology, so the button still announces as "Search" while giving the
        wordmark beside it room to be read. The ⌕ glyph is aria-hidden, so
        without the label the link would announce as nothing at all.
      */}
      <span class="icon-button__label">Search</span>
    </a>
    <ThemeToggle />
  </div>
</header>

<script is:inline src="/header.js" defer></script>
